passgen - Password Generator
=============================

passgen is a command-line password generator written in C. It generates
cryptographically secure random passwords and copies them directly to
your clipboard.


Features
--------

* Generate random passwords with configurable length (4-100 characters)
* Character set includes uppercase, lowercase, digits, and special symbols
* Automatic clipboard integration:
  - X11 (via xclip)
  - Wayland (via wl-copy)
  - macOS (via pbcopy)
* No external dependencies beyond standard system tools


Requirements
------------

* GCC or compatible C compiler
* make
* (optional) xclip or wl-copy for clipboard support on Linux
* (optional) Check library for running tests


Installation
------------

  $ make
  $ sudo make install

This installs the passgen binary to /usr/local/bin by default. To change
the prefix:

  $ make PREFIX=$HOME/.local install


Usage
-----

  $ passgen -g <length>

Generate a password of the specified length:

  $ passgen -g 32
  aB3$xK9#mN8@pQ2&rT5*wY7(zC1)vF4

The generated password is printed to stdout and automatically copied to
your clipboard.

  $ passgen -h

Display help screen.


Options
-------

  -g <len>   Generate a password of <len> characters (4-100)
  -h         Show this help message


Building from source
--------------------

  $ make          Build the project
  $ make test     Build and run tests
  $ make clean    Remove build artifacts
  $ make install  Install to system
  $ make uninstall


Running tests
-------------

Tests use the Check unit testing framework:

  $ make test


Project structure
-----------------

  src/             Source files
  tests/           Test files
  Makefile         Build system
  obj/             Compiled object files (generated)
  bin/             Compiled binaries (generated)


